# Context Management Rules

This repository is a portfolio monorepo. Context must be loaded deliberately so each agent keeps the
project consistent without reading the entire repo on every task.

## Always read first

At the start of a new task, read these files before making changes:

- `README.md`
- `docs/roadmap.md`
- `docs/architecture.md`
- `docs/dependency-graph.md`
- `docs/agent-handoff.md`

If the task is explicitly tiny (for example, "show git status"), this can be skipped.

## Scope profiles

Choose one scope profile before editing.

### App work: `apps/*`

Use this when changing an app UI, feature, route, container, app README, or app behavior.

Read:

- target app `package.json`
- target app `README.md` if it exists
- target app entry files: `src/main.tsx`, `src/app/*`
- relevant feature files only
- shared package READMEs/contracts that the app consumes:
  - `packages/ui/src/index.ts`
  - `packages/sdk/src/index.ts`
  - `packages/hooks/src/index.ts`
  - `packages/mock-network/src/index.ts` when mock transport is involved

Rule: app chats must keep shared package contracts in context. Apps consume `packages/*`; do not
change package APIs from an app task without checking all affected consumers.

### Package work: `packages/*`

Use this when changing SDK, UI, hooks, mock-network, package README, or package tests.

Read:

- target package `package.json`
- target package `README.md` if it exists
- target package `src/index.ts`
- target package tests and nearby implementation files

Apps are not required context for package-only work unless:

- changing a public export or public type
- changing UI component props
- changing SDK/hook behavior used by apps
- debugging a consumer regression

When any of those apply, inspect the affected app usages with `rg`.

### Cross-cutting work

Use this for docs, CI, workspace config, dependency graph, screenshots, or repo hygiene.

Read:

- root `package.json`
- `pnpm-workspace.yaml`
- `.github/workflows/ci.yml` when CI/test behavior is involved
- relevant docs under `docs/`
- `docs/agent-handoff.md`

## Context budget

- Prefer `rg` / `rg --files` to discover relevant files.
- Do not read every file in `apps/` or `packages/` by default.
- Summarize what you learned before broad edits.
- If a change crosses ownership boundaries, state that explicitly in the handoff.
